  "evidenceBoundary": {
    "exact": "Each allowed route composes an existing byte-pinned current-build formatter contract with the maintained finite structural reader. The shared decoder admits only listed physical tags/member counts and exact cursors. Byte-pinned action dependencies admit a first root only when the complete finite grammar rejoins the authenticated top-level cursor. This includes the broad Damage, Effect and FindTarget roots and the lower-frequency exact roots listed in rootTags. Tag 0x0118 pins PlayPerfectDodgeAnim and its six stored fields; C9 additionally pins its switch route and mechanically validated nested SequenceActionData MethodSpec/provider chain.",
    "direct": "The first root is restricted to the listed authenticated routes; every listed root is admitted only where its complete nested body reaches the independent following cursor. Nested and later actions must also be in allowedReachedRoutes. IfElseAction requires the pinned SequenceActionData provider chain; JumpToAction reuses that provider; SetAbilityEntityTarget uses the pinned TargetSettings provider.",
    "structuralOnly": "Anonymous nested member kinds retain the dependency contract boundary; union wrapper identity and record extent are named, while gameplay meaning is not inferred.",
    "unresolved": "Any listed root with an unsupported nested profile remains bounded at its first unresolved child. C9 branches containing subtype-one nested profiles, positive DamageUnit member-ten GameplayTag lists, or positive EffectActionCfg arrays remain bounded and unsupported."
  },
